<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hampshire</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hampshire is a county on the south coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, including the ports of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southampton">Southampton</a> and Portsmouth and the New Forest. Its old capital, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winchester">Winchester</a>, was the chief royal city of the kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wessex">Wessex</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> the area lay within the territories of the Atrebates and Belgae, and the English colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-hampshire">New Hampshire</a> was named after it in the 1620s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hampshire.jpg" alt="Hampshire" width="320" height="222" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ITookSomePhotos · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Spinnaker_Tower,_Portsmouth,_England_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
